schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: The Ethereum Ecosystem
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: guide
  summary: >-
    A grounded, hype-free tour of Ethereum for regenerative communities in East
    Africa and Somaliland: what Ethereum is (a shared, permissionless compute
    platform, not just a currency), Layer 2 networks as a cost/speed fix,
    DeFi (swaps, lending, stablecoins), NFTs as provable digital ownership, and
    DAOs as a new organizational form. Closes with practical low-risk starter
    steps (wallet, L2 browsing, block explorer, browsing a DAO's governance).
  audience: beginner community members and organizers in East Africa / Somaliland
    exploring web3 for the first time
  known_tensions:
    - >-
      The article frames the technology as neutral ("can serve extractive
      finance or regenerative purposes") while also actively encouraging
      exploration of DeFi/DAOs — readers should weigh real risk (smart
      contract bugs, volatility, hacks) against the framed opportunity.
  related_concepts:
    - decentralized-finance-defi
  related_resources:
    - ethereum
    - metamask
    - uniswap
    - base
    - etherscan
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/ethereum-ecosystem.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted

# assessed-but-excluded (wo-b4d86b063d8c, ethereum-ecosystem.md):
